# Writer 12 (session 7c, A2). L §5.14 `on d`: "A day that is a hole and not a window has no bound, so that is every
# span, earlier ones included, whatever the instance's `when` says: its booking cut min(t, K) is a hole with it
# (§5.14.3)." L §5.14.3: "An amount, or a `when`, that was a hole at its cut stays a hole movement until a version
# answers it." A keyed decision (a relabel, `reads x`) whose binding's `on` and own day are the hole hday is a hole
# movement: the balance it reaches is a hole naming hday, as its plan twin's is (triage scratch a2/v18, the leg to
# world and no `reads`, prints these three lines). refcore had crashed with KeyError: 'x' (scratch a2/v16).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in gifts and k.owner == w.giver then 0 else 1, if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
kind gifts: transfers
  attr giver: key persons
  attr receiver: key persons
place k1: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place k2: savings lives 2026-01-01..
index ks = [a, b]
place acct[j in ks]: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input g_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0
  rule gift beats base = if p == m.receiver then 1 else 0 when m in gifts
move w1[x in savings on wage_day]: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to x amount wage_amt
input hday: date
move g[x in savings on hday]: gifts
  on hday
  reads x
  attr giver = tomek
  attr receiver = ania
  leg cash from x to x amount bal(x) of tomek
ask q: bal(k1, 2026-12-31) of ania

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  opening[k1] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[k2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[acct[a]] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[acct[b]] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
  g_day = 2026-03-01
  hday = ?"not yet"
=== expect
q: ?"not yet" (hday)
  unfulfilled: w1[k1]
  cut 2026-12-31
